WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Bearings and lubrication. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Connect load, speed, oil and wear

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Bearings support moving parts and manage contact under load. Lubrication separates surfaces in many operating conditions; it does not remove every loss.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Map shaft load → bearing contact → lubricant film → heat removal, then list what the simple map leaves out.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Choose evidence from scenarios

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Connect load, speed, oil and wear
